more expensive.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL>Classification</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>[Certified,] [Field grown] wildflower sod, machine cut at a uniform thickness of<MET> [25] [_____] mm</MET><ENG> [one] [_____] inch</ENG> within a tolerance of<MET> 6 mm</MET><ENG> 
1/4 inch</ENG>, excluding top growth. Top growth shall be a maximum height of<MET> [75] [_____] mm</MET><ENG> [3] [_____] inches</ENG>.  Each individual wildflower sod piece 
shall be strong enough to support its own weight when lifted by the ends.  Broken pads, irregular shaped pieces, and torn or uneven ends will be 
rejected.  [Wood pegs and wire staples for anchorage on slope conditions, three to one or greater, shall be used as recommended by wildflower sod 
supplier.]</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
